<blockquote class="uncited"><div>With the latest CPS-Software i can go in the "OpenGD77 Support" Mode. If i click "Backup settings" the radio switch an shows me the screen with two frequencies and the computer save a setting.dat file.</div></blockquote>I've never heard of "OpenGD77 Support" mode or "Backup settings" in the official CPS<br><br>This must be something new they added. We have no communcation with Radioddity, so have no idea what these functions do<br><br><br>As Daniel has stated in his email, Radioddity have a bad track record for screwing up the lock / signature bytes that the bootloader examines to determine whether it will reload new firmware.<br><br>If these bytes are ever erased, the radio will no longer be able to be updated, without it being disassembled and the CPU completely erased and a modified version of the bootloader being installed using a hardware programmer tool, like JLink.<br><br><br>Anyway, it sounds like you never installed the OpenGD77 firmware on this radio, and all the problems you are experiencing are with new versions of the official firmware.<br><br>So I don't understand why you posted the question to this forum which is exclusively for the OpenGD77 firmware<br><br>Please can you confirm if you are using the OpenGD77 firmware, and if not, you need to contact Radioddity<br><br>Note. I have now moved this thread to the Off Topic section, as it does not appear to be related to the OpenGD77 firmware or CPS<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Thu Jul 13, 2023 7:43 am</p><hr />
