<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hi,<br><br>  I would add à reminder here:<br><strong class="text-strong">Never do à factory reset on GD-77/DM-1801/RD-5R, depending on the official (manufacturer) firmware, it will kill the protection bytes and turn the radio into something you cannot flash anymore unless you flash a modified bootloader using a hardware programmer.</strong><br><br>Cheers.<br>---<br>Daniel</div></blockquote>Someytimes also just changing to a different version of official firmware has been known to erase the protection bytes, however its unclear exactly when this happens, i.e which versions of official firmware do this and under what conditions<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Thu Jul 13, 2023 6:00 am</p><hr />
