		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3027&amp;p=24360#p24360"><![CDATA[
Unfortunately you are confusing things by switching back and forward between OpenGD77 and the radioddity firmware. You can't do that without the chance of problems. You must always use the correct download program.  For the .sgl files from radioddity you must use update.exe, for the .bin files from OpenGD77 you must the the OpenGD77 CPS. <br><br>When loading OpenGD77 and the radio said "Settings Update" you should press the green key to acknowledge and it should then work OK.  If it still doesn't respond then it sounds like you may have a hardware problem. <br><br>Colin G4EML.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Wed Jul 12, 2023 3:12 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
